so you guys have heard about Dr fosey  Khan talking about how to find bugs from  Deep learning programs and I will then  talk about how to figure out what goes  wrong figure out the root causes of the  this box  so this stays AI artificial intelligence  has been increasingly embedded into  modern software application that and the  systems and the key enabler behind this  is deep learning and you know deep  learning is quite different from  traditional software engineering in  traditional software development we  programmers manually write the program  logic in source code right but in deep  learning the models actually learn their  own logic from the training data and  also in traditional software development  everything is encoded in symbolic  representations right data structures  etc etc  but in deep learning things are encoded  into high dimensional arrays and there  is a lot of calculus and linear algebra  operations over this arrays to make the  inference  this brings a lot of challenge to debug  deep learning models  you know in the old world traditional  software if we want to debug error we  basically set a breakpoint and we can  step through each line of code to figure  out the root cause of this error  but in deep learning for neural net how  do we even set a breakpoint  even if sometimes we can actually peek  into the internal you know a specific  layer or neuron in the neural NAB but  what we can get from at the runtime the  runtime values we get from this neural  net are high dimensional arrays which  are hard to interpret right  all right let's actually look at one  example suppose you're a programmer and  you actually Trend this recurrent neural  network to classify ready comments to  positive or negative opinions  and you find out the model accuracy is  pretty low and you are wondering why  right so for example this comment  clearly shares a negative opinion but  the model misclassifies it as positive  so it's really hard to tell exactly what  happens inside the model right and why  this error occurs  and this is actually why some people you  know actually call Deep learning Alchemy  right people don't know exactly why  something works and why something  doesn't work okay it's like a giant  black box to us to programmers  our solution is to transform this  complex and familiar neural network back  to something we are familiar with right  like uh Finance day machine and in this  way we can bring back all the good stuff  we have in the traditional programming  world like people can step through each  state in the financial State machine and  inspect the state value  um in the in the financial State machine  So based on this idea we actually build  a debugging tool called The Deep seer in  the middle of this interface is a  visualization of the finite State  machine abstracted from an RN model and  it provides programmers a bird's eye  view of what's already going on in the  internal decision making process of the  model  and the model reads each word in input  text it will Transit between different  state until it reach to the end of the  text to make it the final decision  and if you click on state you can  actually see the frequent words and  phrases associated with this state so in  this way we convert those  uninterpretable High dimensional arrays  into a symbolic representation that are  interpretable to programmers  and you can also dig into individual  data points in the training data search  and filter and Trace all the way back to  the state diagram  going back to the previous  misclassification example with dips here  you can actually enter this  misclassified text into deep Seer and  deepseer will immediately produce a  state Trace that reflects the  intermediate decisions made by the iron  model after reading each word in the  input text here red means negative and  blue means positive similar to how you  step through a program The Source Code  you can step through this state trace  and look at what 